# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale tr
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as the morning band.
# Surface: noun/adverb 'morning' (distinct from 'yarın' = tomorrow) -- the deictic form these phrases use.
# Source: Wiktionary, sabah — https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sabah#Turkish
sabah
# Surface: 3rd-person possessive "sabahı" ("its morning" / "the morning of
# <day>") -- the form the "<weekday> sabahı [saat ...]" construction uses
# ("salı sabahı saat 9'da" = "Tuesday morning at 9"). Same band as "sabah";
# Source: TDK Güncel Türkçe Sözlük, "sabah" + 3sg possessive -ı.
sabahı
